<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --card-hover: #22263a;
    --accent: #4f8cff;
    --accent2: #ff6b6b;
    --accent3: #ffd93d;
    --accent4: #6bcb77;
    --text: #e0e0e0;
    --text-muted: #8a8fa8;
    --border: #2a2e3f;
    --red: #ff4757;
    --orange: #ffa502;
    --green: #2ed573;
    --iran: #8e44ad;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 56px 20px 36px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2)); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero .subtitle { font-size: 1em; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .hero .date-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero .war-day { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent2); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 8px; }
  .hero .build-meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .triplet-badge { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #0e1a1e); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--accent); display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }

  .direction-of-travel { max-width: 900px; margin: 24px auto; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #1a1d27); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 28px; font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.55; }
  .direction-of-travel .label { font-size: 0.72em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .direction-of-travel .body { color: var(--text); }
  .direction-of-travel .body .cite { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move { border-color: var(--border); }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move .body { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }

  .disclaimer { background: #2a1a1a; border: 1px solid #5a2020; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px auto; max-width: 900px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #ffaaaa; }
  .disclaimer strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .section { padding: 30px 0; }
  .section-title { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .section-title .meta { font-size: 0.6em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }

  .forecast-board { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label { font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 14px 0 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .forecast-card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; }
  .forecast-card.cat-diplomacy { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card.cat-military { border-left-color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card.cat-regime { border-left-color: var(--iran); }
  .forecast-card.cat-market { border-left-color: var(--accent3); }
  .forecast-card.cat-domestic { border-left-color: var(--accent4); }
  .forecast-card.cat-humanitarian { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-id { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-category { font-size: 0.7em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-question { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .forecast-card .fc-probrow { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-up { color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-down { color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.no-move { color: var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-horizon { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta-reason { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dd { color: var(--text); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicators { font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 2px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-OBSERVED { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); border-color: var(--green); color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-PARTIAL { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); border-color: var(--orange); color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-CONTRADICTED { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-NOT_OBSERVED { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE { opacity: 0.55; border-left-style: dashed; }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE .fc-question::after { content: ' [OBE]'; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .forecast-empty-slot { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  .delta-narrative p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .delta-narrative p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .delta-narrative p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  .scenario-map { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .prob-bar-container { display: flex; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .prob-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85em; color: #fff; }
  .prob-escalation { background: var(--red); }
  .prob-status { background: var(--orange); }
  .prob-deescalation { background: var(--green); }
  .scenario-line { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .scenario-line strong.label-esc { color: var(--red); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-prot { color: var(--orange); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-desc { color: var(--green); }

  .inside-iran { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .inside-iran p { font-size: 0.93em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .inside-iran p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .iran-media-badges { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .iran-media-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72em; color: var(--iran); }

  .regime-watch { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .regime-watch-meta { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .regime-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .regime-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .regime-row .name { font-weight: 600; }
  .regime-row .p { font-size: 1.4em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--orange); }
  .regime-row .drivers { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); flex-basis: 100%; margin-top: 4px; }

  .sources-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .sources-list li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.88em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .sources-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-tier { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.5px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .source-tier.tier-TIER1 { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid var(--green); }
  .source-tier.tier-OSINT { background: rgba(79, 140, 255, 0.15); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .source-tier.tier-STATE_MEDIA { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); color: var(--orange); border: 1px solid var(--orange); }
  .source-tier.tier-EXPERT { background: rgba(155, 89, 182, 0.15); color: #9b59b6; border: 1px solid #9b59b6; }

  .expert-appendix { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .expert-appendix summary { padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92em; user-select: none; }
  .expert-appendix summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .expert-appendix[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 20px 18px; }
  .expert-quote { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .expert-quote .expert-name { font-weight: 700; color: #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .expert-empty { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  footer { text-align: center; padding: 32px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8em; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 32px; }
  footer .next-update { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero { padding: 36px 16px 24px; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.3; }
    .container { padding: 12px; }
    .direction-of-travel { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 0.95em; }
    .disclaimer { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 12px; font-size: 0.8em; }
    .section-title { font-size: 1.2em; }
    .forecast-card { padding: 14px 16px; }
    .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.5em; }
    .scenario-map, .inside-iran, .regime-watch, .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Forecast board + descriptive delta. Predictions are time-bounded and scored; descriptions are sourced and verb-disciplined.</p>
  <span class="date-badge">July 5, 2026</span>
  <span class="war-day">Day 128</span>
  <div class="build-meta">Published: <span id="pub-ts">2026-07-05 (automated draft)</span> · Build <span id="build-id" style="font-family:monospace;opacity:0.6;">v48.0</span></div>
  <div class="triplet-badge">⚖ Triple-blind: Analyst + Devil's Advocate + Judge · forecast-board v45 · Sunday cold-start audit</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- 1. DIRECTION OF TRAVEL -->
  <div class="direction-of-travel">
    <div class="label">Where this is heading</div>
    <div class="body">
      Israeli coalition dissolution closed to 72% (<span class="cite">F7</span>) following the Knesset legal adviser's July 17 recommendation and Edelstein's Likud departure reducing the coalition below the 61-seat threshold, while the post-funeral US-Iran round (<span class="cite">F8</span>: 62%) defines the next 15-day decision node and Hormuz commercial recovery (<span class="cite">F9</span>: 25%) remains structurally constrained by active mining despite the June 17 MOU framework.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <strong>⚠ DISCLAIMER:</strong> This analysis relies on open sources (OSINT) and AI-generated assessments. Probabilities are time-bounded forecasts with resolution criteria; track record visible internally until ≥20 forecasts resolve. Descriptive sections enforce verb discipline — any causal/directional claim must cite a forecast or be marked context-only.
  </div>

  <!-- 2. FORECAST BOARD -->
  <div class="section" id="forecast-board">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Forecast Board
      <span class="meta">4 active · last reasoned 2026-07-05 · Sunday cold-start audit · 5 resolved this run</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="forecast-board">

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">NEAR-TERM · ≤72h</div>
      <div class="forecast-empty-slot">No publishable forecast in this horizon today.</div>

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">7–30 DAYS</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F6</span>
          <span class="fc-category">domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the Knesset pass the dissolution bill's final reading with a fixed election date earlier than 2026-10-27 before EOD 2026-07-15?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">22%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">↓ 23pp from 45% (2026-06-02) · cold-start</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-07-15</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Sunday cold-start (p_inherited=0.45, p_cold=0.22, gap=23pp; Judge selects 0.22). Dissolution bill at first reading (106-0, June 1) with no second or third reading scheduled as of July 5. Knesset legal adviser recommended July 17 dissolution — leaving effectively zero parliamentary days for two more readings before the July 15 horizon. Coalition advanced a separate Basic Law shielding Haredi draft evaders on July 1, consuming floor time. Haredi date-dispute unresolved. Primary YES scenario: coalition whips both Haredi blocs into compressed readings within 10 days — low-probability given scheduling void.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if the Knesset passes the dissolution bill in final (third) reading AND specifies a fixed election date earlier than 2026-10-27, before EOD 2026-07-15.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Two TIER1 (Times of Israel/Reuters/AP/JPost) citing the Knesset plenum vote record.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>First/second readings without final passage = NO count. Passage leaving date to later committee = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Fixed date ≥ Oct 27 = NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Plenum third-reading dissolution vote with fixed date</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Haredi-coalition agreement on fixed election date</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F8</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the US-Iran negotiating round scheduled to resume after the Khamenei funeral (~July 11) produce a publicly confirmed joint outcome statement or an agreed next-meeting date, published by a named mediator (Qatar or Pakistan), before EOD 2026-07-20?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">62%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-07-20</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New. Doha technical talks (June 30–July 2) produced positive progress per Qatar, established a US-Iran communication channel, and both parties agreed to resume after the Khamenei funeral (~July 9). VP Vance: "talks are going well" (July 1). Named mediators Qatar and Pakistan active. Primary risk: anti-US funeral rhetoric (calls for Trump's death, July 5) could harden Iranian domestic constraints on visible publicly-confirmable progress.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if a named Qatari or Pakistani official, or a named US or Iranian principal, publicly confirms a joint outcome statement or a specific next-round date, published by Reuters/AP/AFP/Al Jazeera/IRNA before EOD 2026-07-20.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>TIER1: Reuters, AP, AFP, Al Jazeera, IRNA, NPR, CBS. Named Qatari/Pakistani official confirmation required. Unilateral Trump claim without mediator confirmation does NOT resolve YES.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Talks with no public output (quiet continuation) = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. One side claims progress without mediator confirmation = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Qatar or Pakistan FM confirms post-funeral talks held</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Witkoff or Gharibabadi named in TIER1 on resumed session</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Khamenei funeral ends without diplomatic rupture (~July 9)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30–90 DAYS</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-market status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F9</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will a 7-day rolling average of ≥50 commercial transits/day through the Strait of Hormuz be recorded in IMF PortWatch or equivalent AIS-based data before EOD 2026-08-15?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">25%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-08-15</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New; successor to RESOLVED-NO F4. PortWatch 7-day MA ~13–27 transits/day (June 21–July 2); single-day high of 39 on July 3 (highest post-war but still well below threshold). Pre-war baseline ~84/day. ~80 mines remain in the strait; CENTCOM demining active but slow. Iran's July 4 fee declaration creates commercial uncertainty post-Aug 16. Reaching 50/day requires ~4× acceleration in 41 days — possible if the inbound lane is cleared by late July, but not the base case.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if IMF PortWatch 7-day moving average equals or exceeds 50 commercial transits/day for any 7-day window ending on or before 2026-08-15. Naval-escorted commercial vessels count. Military-only movements do not count.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Primary: IMF PortWatch (portwatch.imf.org). Secondary: Windward AIS, Lloyd's List. If PortWatch shows ≥50 and AIS-dark >15% suspected, apply 15% haircut; if adjusted count still ≥50, resolve YES.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Data gap >5 days in PortWatch: use Windward/Lloyd's. AIS-dark rates >30% (spoofing): AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IMF PortWatch 7-day MA exceeds 30/day (necessary but not sufficient)</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Lloyd's or Windward publishes Hormuz clearance-lane announcement</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran halts or delays fee implementation post-Aug 16</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">6–12 MONTHS</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-regime status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F7</span>
          <span class="fc-category">regime</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Netanyahu's coalition lose its Knesset majority or dissolve early before 2026-10-27?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">72%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-up">↑ 37pp from 35% (2026-05-11) · cold-start · 47d stale</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-27</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Sunday cold-start audit (p_inherited=0.35, p_cold=0.72, gap=37pp; 47-day staleness — prior estimate methodologically invalid). Judge selects 0.72. Three compounding factors: (1) coalition at 60 seats following Yuli Edelstein's Likud departure July 2 to form Edelstein-Shaked alliance — below the 61-seat majority threshold in the 120-seat Knesset; (2) Knesset legal adviser formally recommended July 17 dissolution; (3) Hamas explicitly cited Israeli elections as reason to delay Gaza reconstruction talks, confirming external actors treat early dissolution as base case. Resolution requires a formal Knesset roll-call vote or dissolution bill passage through second/third readings — no formal vote yet; ACTIVE maintained.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if a Knesset roll-call vote confirms coalition loss of majority (fewer than 61 seats documented) OR the Knesset passes the dissolution bill on second and third readings scheduling early elections, confirmed by official Knesset record or TIER1, before EOD 2026-10-27.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Knesset official record + Reuters/Haaretz/Times of Israel. Polling alone does not resolve.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Coalition drops below 61 seats but Netanyahu remains caretaker: RESOLVE-YES. Netanyahu resigns without formal vote: RESOLVE-YES if TIER1. Elections held and Netanyahu wins with new coalition: RESOLVE-YES (original coalition collapsed). No dissolution or majority vote by Oct 27: RESOLVE-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Formal Knesset roll-call vote confirming majority loss</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Dissolution bill passes second and third reading (~July 17)</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-PARTIAL">Additional documented coalition defections (Edelstein July 2: coalition at 60 seats)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 3. 24-48H DELTA -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>On June 17, US President Trump and Iranian President Pezeshkian signed the 14-point Islamabad Memorandum of Understanding, with Trump signing at Versailles during the G7 and Pezeshkian signing in Tehran. The MOU established a 60-day negotiation framework covering Hormuz freedom of navigation, Iran's nuclear and missile programs, and sanctions relief. It required Iran to clear Hormuz mines within 30 days and called for a cessation of hostilities across all fronts, including Lebanon. The signing immediately superseded Iran's June 1 negotiation suspension — a Pakistan-hosted facilitated session (June 12–14) with named principals Witkoff and Araghchi produced the MOU text before EOD June 16. → moved <span class="cite">F1</span>, <span class="cite">F2</span></p>

      <p>The post-MOU period produced direct bilateral military exchanges within the June 10–24 forecast window. After the MOU signing, Israel struck a radar installation near Tehran in response to claimed Iranian violations; Iran responded by firing two missiles at Israeli cities and an additional salvo at Beer Sheva. The exchange involved Israeli strikes on Iranian territory and Iranian strikes on Israeli cities within a single rolling 48-hour period, confirmed by NPR, CNN, and Al Jazeera. The ceasefire held by June 24, in part due to direct US intervention with Netanyahu. → moved <span class="cite">F3</span></p>

      <p>Hormuz commercial traffic failed to approach the 50-transit threshold throughout the June 2–July 2 period. IMF PortWatch recorded a 7-day moving average of 13.14 on June 21. On July 3, single-day transits reached 39 vessels — the highest post-war count but still below half the pre-war ~84/day baseline. The strait remains physically obstructed by approximately 80 Iranian mines (Maham-3 and Maham-7 types per expert estimates). CENTCOM confirmed an active mine clearance mission with USS Frank E. Peterson and USS Michael Murphy as lead assets, France and the UK leading the international MCM coalition under MOU terms. On July 4, Iran's ambassador to China declared that navigation fees "will definitely" be charged once the 60-day free-passage window expires (~Aug 16), a position the US has rejected. → moved <span class="cite">F4</span>, <span class="cite">F5</span>, supports <span class="cite">F9</span> without move</p>

      <p>US and Iranian technical negotiators held two days of indirect talks in Doha (June 30–July 2). The US side (Witkoff, Kushner) met separately with Qatari Emir Sheikh Tamim, while Iran's Deputy FM Gharibabadi met with Qatari and Pakistani mediators in a parallel track. Qatar announced "positive progress" on Hormuz navigation disputes and Iran's $6 billion in frozen funds. Both sides agreed to establish a formal communication channel and to schedule the next round after the Khamenei funeral concludes. NPR (July 2) confirmed the parties "agreed to continue discussions." Negotiations formally paused July 3–9 for the funeral; the next structured round is expected July 11. → supports <span class="cite">F8</span> without move</p>

      <p>Inside Israel, the Knesset dissolution bill remained at first reading (106-0, June 1) with no second or third reading scheduled as of July 5. The Knesset legal adviser formally recommended a July 17 dissolution — implying final readings would need to occur within days. On July 1, the coalition advanced a separate Basic Law shielding Haredi draft evaders from sanctions, consuming floor time and deepening the Haredi-secular rift. Yuli Edelstein left Likud on July 2 to pursue a new right-wing alliance with Ayelet Shaked, a visible fracturing of the ruling party ahead of elections. Hamas confirmed it is deliberately slowing Gaza reconstruction talks pending Israeli election results — external confirmation that market actors treat early dissolution as the base case. → moved <span class="cite">F6</span>, <span class="cite">F7</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 4. SCENARIO MAP -->
  <div class="section" id="scenario-map">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Scenario Map
      <span class="meta">Computed from Forecast Board · 1 sentence per scenario</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="scenario-map">
      <div class="prob-bar-container">
        <div class="prob-bar prob-escalation" style="width:20%;">Escalation 20%</div>
        <div class="prob-bar prob-status" style="width:45%;">Protracted 45%</div>
        <div class="prob-bar prob-deescalation" style="width:35%;">De-esc 35%</div>
      </div>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path:</strong> F8 fails to produce a public joint outcome after the Khamenei funeral — driven by hardened domestic anti-US constraints or an Israeli military action timed to the coalition's election campaign (F7: 72%) — triggering MOU diplomatic rupture before demining produces commercial normalization (F9: 25%).</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path:</strong> Post-funeral talks resume but produce no TIER1-confirmed public output (F8 resolves NO per ambiguity rule), Hormuz demining advances below the 50-transit threshold through August 15 (F9 NO), and Israeli dissolution proceeds (F7) without external recalculation, leaving the MOU framework legally intact but commercially and diplomatically stalled.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path:</strong> Qatar or Pakistan FM confirms a joint outcome and specific next-round date after the expected July 11 resumption (F8 YES), enabling IAEA and Hormuz normalization tracks to advance toward the 50-transit threshold (F9 trajectory), while Israeli elections (F7) produce a coalition less structurally invested in blocking Gaza reconstruction engagement.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 5. INSIDE IRAN -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · 200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>Iran's state media apparatus (IRNA, Tasnim, PressTV) framed the delayed state funeral of Ali Khamenei (July 3–9) as a demonstration of the Islamic Republic's continuity and popular legitimacy. The four-month delay — attributed officially to "war conditions" and "the brutal US invasion" — was presented as evidence that the Republic endured an existential assault and survived. IRNA reported between 15 and 20 million expected mourners across Tehran, Qom, Najaf, Karbala, and Mashhad. The presence of IRGC Chief and Quds Force leadership at the funeral ceremonies was broadcast prominently, re-centering the Revolutionary Guard as the institutional backbone of the post-Khamenei order under new Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei (in office since March 9). → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

      <p>A performer at the July 5 Tehran ceremony called publicly for Trump's death to crowd applause, covered without editorial distance on state channels — the anti-US framing of the MOU period is sustained even as technical negotiators sit in Doha. On Hormuz fees, IRNA and Tasnim amplified Ambassador statements framing navigation charges as sovereign rights under UNCLOS and international practice, not a violation of the MOU's 60-day free-passage clause. The $6 billion frozen funds issue was presented as a US debt, not a negotiating concession, in all state coverage of the Doha talks. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

      <p>Domestically, coverage of the Pezeshkian government's role in the reconstruction framework was cautiously positive, but Mojtaba Khamenei has not yet publicly endorsed the MOU framework — state media language remains that the talks are being "supervised" by the new leadership, not endorsed. This framing shapes the domestic political space in which the post-funeral round must produce visible progress. → supports <span class="cite">F8</span> without move</p>
    </div>
  </div>

